<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: German, Japanese firms to invest in Ireland.</title>
<headline>German, Japanese firms to invest in Ireland.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial development agency IDA Ireland said on Thursday that Deutsches Reiseburo, Germany's largest travel agency and fourth largest tour operator, will establish a shared services and teleservices centre in Galway, Ireland.</p>
<p>Deutsches Reiseburo is owned by German airline Lufthansa and Deutsche Bahn, the German railway.</p>
<p>The centre will create 175 new jobs within three years, mainly for people with fluency in German, IDA Ireland said in a statement.</p>
<p>It also announced that KAO Corporation, Japan's largest manufacturer of household products, plans to invest a total of 14 million Irish pounds in a major expansion of its Dublin-based operations.</p>
<p>The investment will create 300 new jobs within three years - 200 in CD-ROM production and 100 in a teleservices centre.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
